@* ProductDetail.razor — Phase 3.2 (rewritten for staff edit + customer view)

   Product detail page at route `/Products/{Id:guid}`. Reached from the
   Products grid by clicking a product card. ALL authenticated users can
   view this page — the role determines what they see + can do.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   TWO VIEWS BASED ON ROLE
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   CUSTOMER VIEW (Customer role, and anyone not in Admin/Manager/Employee):
     - Breadcrumb: Products → [Category / Sub / SubSub] → [Product Name]
     - Product picture (or placeholder)
     - Product name (read-only)
     - Price (read-only)
     - Description (read-only)
     - Category hierarchy label (Category › SubCategory › SubSubCategory)
     - Quantity selector (1 to MyPurchaseLimit, if a limit applies)
     - Add to Cart button
     - NO stock number is shown.
     - NO groups, NO purchase limits, NO internal audit details.

   STAFF VIEW (Admin, Manager, Employee — authorized by [RequireRoles]
   on the command handlers themselves; the page just checks role via
   AuthenticationStateProvider to decide what UI to render):
     Everything in the customer view EXCEPT the staff sees additional
     edit affordances below the read-only display:
       1. Change Photo button → opens the same dropzone + preview card UI
          used on CreateProduct.razor. Same JPEG/PNG/WebP + 5 MB rules.
          On save: (a) upload new file via IFileStorage.SaveAsync,
                   (b) delete the OLD file via IFileStorage.DeleteAsync
                       (hard delete — orphaned images are cleaned up),
                   (c) dispatch UpdateProductDetailsCommand with the new
                       PictureUrl + the existing Name/Description/Price
                       (UpdateProductDetails is the only command that
                       can change PictureUrl).
       2. Edit Name + Description → two text inputs + Save button.
          Dispatches UpdateProductDetailsCommand with the new values
          (PictureUrl is passed as the existing value — unchanged).
       3. Per-group purchase limits editor:
          - Loads ALL existing group names via GetAllGroupNamesQuery
            (every existing group must have a limit OR be explicitly
            set to "no limit" by leaving the field empty + clicking
            "Remove limit").
          - For each existing limit on this product, shows a row with
            the group name (read-only) + the current limit (editable
            RadzenNumeric) + a Save button per row.
          - For each existing group that has NO limit set on this
            product, shows a row with the group name + an empty limit
            input + a "Set limit" button.
          - "Add custom group" button below the list lets staff set a
            limit for a group name that doesn't have any users yet
            (forward-looking). Mirrors CreateProduct's pattern.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   ROLE CHECK
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Uses AuthenticationStateProvider (NOT ICurrentUserService.IsInRole)
   because in interactive Blazor Server mode, ICurrentUserService reads
   from IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext which is null over the SignalR
   circuit. Same pattern as Sales.razor + SaleDetail.razor.

   The backend command handlers ALSO enforce [RequireRoles] as
   defense-in-depth — even if a non-staff user could see the buttons,
   the handler would reject the dispatch.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   IMAGE UPLOAD FLOW (mirrors CreateProduct.razor — same rules)
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   - Dropzone + InputFile with accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp".
   - Validates content type + 5 MB max size client-side.
   - Buffers the bytes IMMEDIATELY in OnInputFileChange (not at submit
     time) to avoid the JSException that occurs when the JS-side
     _blazorFilesById registry is cleared by Hot Reload / circuit
     reconnect / runtime housekeeping.
   - Generates a downscaled data: URL preview (400×400 max) via
     IBrowserFile.RequestImageFileAsync.
   - On "Save photo": stream bytes to IFileStorage.SaveAsync → get URL,
     then IFileStorage.DeleteAsync(oldPictureUrl) to hard-delete the
     previous file, then dispatch UpdateProductDetailsCommand with
     new PictureUrl + existing Name/Description/Price.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   LOCALIZATION
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   All user-visible strings via IStringLocalizer<ProductDetail> (Loc).
   Keys in ProductDetail.fa-IR.resx + ProductDetail.en-US.resx.
   RTL handled at the <html dir> level by MainLayout.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   TIMEZONE (Tehran, not UTC)
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   No timestamps displayed on this page currently. If timestamps are
   added in the future, use the same inline +3:30 offset arithmetic
   used in Sales.razor / SaleDetail.razor. Server runs in UTC; using
   .LocalDateTime would show UTC times instead of Tehran times.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All buttons are regular RadzenButtons
     with async Click handlers that dispatch commands via Wolverine.
     The Blazor circuit's anti-forgery token is established at circuit
     start. No form POST happens.

   ROUTE PARAMETER:
     `Id` is a Guid bound from the URL via [Parameter]. The @page
     constraint `{Id:guid}` validates the URL segment is parseable as
     a Guid before this component even loads — a malformed URL gets a
     404 from the router, not a runtime exception here. *@

@page "/Products/{Id:guid}"
@attribute [Authorize]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Interfaces
@using TakOne.Application.Products.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Queries.GetProductById
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.UpdateProductDetails
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.SetProductPurchaseLimit
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.RemoveProductPurchaseLimit
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Queries.GetCategoryByIdWithHierarchy
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.CreateOrAppendSale
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Queries.GetAllGroupNames
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<ProductDetail> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject IFileStorage FileStorage

<PageTitle>@(_product is null ? Loc["PageTitle"] : $"{_product.Name} — TakOne")</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            /* Layout — 12-col grid on desktop/tablet, stacks on mobile */
            .detail-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
                gap: 2rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 768px) {
                .detail-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1.25rem;
                }
            }

            /* Picture — square aspect ratio, placeholder-friendly. */
            .detail-picture {
                position: relative;
                aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                border-radius: var(--rz-border-radius);
                overflow: hidden;
                max-width: 480px;
            }

                .detail-picture img {
                    width: 100%;
                    height: 100%;
                    object-fit: contain;
                }

                .detail-picture .rz-icon {
                    font-size: 8rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                }

            /* "Change photo" button — overlaid on the picture bottom-right
                           corner. Only shown to staff. Uses RadzenButton underneath
                           but is positioned via a wrapper. */
            .change-photo-overlay {
                position: absolute;
                inset-inline-end: 0.5rem;
                bottom: 0.5rem;
            }

            /* Purchase panel — the right column */
            .detail-info {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 1rem;
            }

            .detail-name {
                font-size: 1.6rem;
                font-weight: 700;
                margin: 0;
                line-height: 1.2;
            }

            .detail-price {
                font-size: 1.75rem;
                font-weight: 700;
                color: var(--rz-primary);
                line-height: 1;
            }

            .detail-description {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                line-height: 1.6;
                white-space: pre-wrap; /* preserves newlines in description */
            }

            /* Category hierarchy chip — small inline label */
            .category-hierarchy {
                display: flex;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
            }

                .category-hierarchy .crumb-sep {
                    opacity: 0.5;
                }

            /* Quantity selector + Add-to-cart button row */
            .purchase-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                align-items: stretch;
                margin-top: 0.5rem;
            }

                .purchase-row .qty-input {
                    width: 100px;
                }

                .purchase-row .add-to-cart-btn {
                    flex: 1;
                }

            @@media (max-width: 480px) {
                .purchase-row {
                    flex-direction: column;
                }

                    .purchase-row .qty-input {
                        width: 100%;
                    }
            }

            /* Breadcrumb */
            .breadcrumb {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                font-size: 0.85rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

                .breadcrumb a {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    text-decoration: none;
                }

                    .breadcrumb a:hover {
                        color: var(--rz-primary);
                        text-decoration: underline;
                    }

                .breadcrumb .crumb-current {
                    color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                    font-weight: 600;
                }

                .breadcrumb .crumb-sep {
                    opacity: 0.5;
                }

            /* ── STAFF EDIT SECTION ────────────────────────────────────── */
            .staff-section {
                border-top: 1px dashed var(--rz-base-border-color);
                padding-top: 1.5rem;
                margin-top: 1.5rem;
            }

            .staff-section-title {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
            }

            .edit-row {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                margin-bottom: 1rem;
            }

            .edit-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
            }

            /* Picture upload section — dropzone + preview card.
                           Mirrors CreateProduct.razor's picture-dropzone styles so the
                           two pages share a consistent upload UI. */
            .upload-section {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.75rem;
            }

            .field-label {
                display: block;
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                font-weight: 500;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
            }

            .picture-dropzone {
                display: block;
                cursor: pointer;
                border: 2px dashed var(--rz-border-color);
                border-radius: 8px;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
                text-align: center;
                transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background-color 0.15s ease;
            }

                .picture-dropzone:hover {
                    border-color: var(--rz-primary);
                    background-color: var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(0, 100, 250, 0.04));
                }

                .picture-dropzone:focus-within {
                    border-color: var(--rz-primary);
                    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(0, 100, 250, 0.15);
                    outline: none;
                }

            .picture-dropzone-input {
                position: absolute;
                width: 1px;
                height: 1px;
                padding: 0;
                margin: -1px;
                overflow: hidden;
                clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
                white-space: nowrap;
                border: 0;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-body {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                pointer-events: none;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-text {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.25rem;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-title {
                font-weight: 600;
                color: var(--rz-text-color);
                font-size: 0.95rem;
            }

            .picture-dropzone-hint {
                font-size: 0.8rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
            }

            .upload-card {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 1rem;
                padding: 1rem;
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color);
                border-radius: 8px;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
            }

            .upload-preview {
                width: 96px;
                height: 96px;
                object-fit: cover;
                border-radius: 6px;
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color);
                flex-shrink: 0;
            }

            .upload-preview-placeholder {
                width: 96px;
                height: 96px;
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                border-radius: 6px;
                border: 1px dashed var(--rz-border-color);
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 2rem;
                flex-shrink: 0;
            }

            .upload-info {
                flex: 1 1 auto;
                min-width: 0;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.25rem;
            }

                .upload-info .file-name {
                    font-weight: 500;
                    overflow: hidden;
                    text-overflow: ellipsis;
                    white-space: nowrap;
                    color: var(--rz-text-color);
                }

                .upload-info .file-size {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    font-size: 0.85rem;
                }

            /* Purchase-limits editor — same row shape as CreateProduct */
            .limit-row {
                display: flex;
                align-items: end;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            }

                .limit-row > * {
                    flex: 0 0 auto;
                }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Back button ──
       Always visible. Returns to /Products. *@
    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToCatalog"]"
                  Icon="arrow_back"
                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                  Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Products", forceLoad: false))" />

    @* ── Loading state ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["Loading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Error state ── *@
    else if (_loadError is not null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Not found ── *@
    else if (_product is null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["NotFoundTitle"]"
                     Text="@Loc["NotFoundMessage"]"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Main content ── *@
    else
    {
        <div class="detail-grid">
            @* LEFT — picture (or placeholder) + staff-only "Change photo" button *@
            <div class="detail-picture">
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_product.PictureUrl))
                {
                    <img src="@_product.PictureUrl" alt="@_product.Name" loading="lazy" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <RadzenIcon Icon="inventory_2" />
                }

                @* Staff-only "Change photo" overlay button — opens the same dropzone
                   UI used on CreateProduct.razor. Only rendered for staff (Admin /
                   Manager / Employee) — same role check as the rest of the staff
                   edit section below. *@
                @if (_canEdit)
                {
                    <div class="change-photo-overlay">
                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ChangePhoto"]"
                                      Icon="photo_camera"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                                      Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                      Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                      Click="@(() => _isPhotoEditorOpen = true)" />
                    </div>
                }
            </div>

            @* RIGHT — info + purchase panel + staff-only edit section *@
            <div class="detail-info">
                @* Breadcrumb: Products → [Category Name] → [Product Name] *@
                <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="breadcrumb">
                    <a href="/Products">@Loc["BreadcrumbProducts"]</a>
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_categoryHierarchy))
                    {
                        <span class="crumb-sep">/</span>
                        <span>@_categoryHierarchy</span>
                    }
                    <span class="crumb-sep">/</span>
                    <span class="crumb-current">@_product.Name</span>
                </nav>

                @* Product name *@
                <h1 class="detail-name">@_product.Name</h1>

                @* Price *@
                <div class="detail-price">@FormatPrice(_product.Price)</div>

                @* Description *@
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_product.Description))
                {
                    <p class="detail-description">@_product.Description</p>
                }

                @* Category hierarchy chip — shown to everyone (customer + staff).
                   Displays Category › SubCategory › SubSubCategory as a small
                   inline label so the customer can verify the categorization
                   without leaving the page. *@
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_categoryHierarchy))
                {
                    <div class="category-hierarchy">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="category" Style="font-size: 1rem;" />
                        <span>@_categoryHierarchy</span>
                    </div>
                }

                @* Customer purchase panel: quantity selector + Add to cart button.
                   Available to ALL authenticated users (every role can buy).
                   Min=1, Max = the per-group limit if one applies to the current
                   user, otherwise a large number (bounded only by stock — staff
                   see no stock number, so the selector's Max here is effectively
                   unlimited).

                   NOTE: _myPurchaseLimit is now populated from
                   _product.MyPurchaseLimit (set by GetProductByIdQueryHandler
                   via Product.GetPurchaseLimitForGroup(currentUser.GroupName)).
                   Before this fix, _myPurchaseLimit was hardcoded to null
                   because ProductDto didn't expose the field — so the
                   selector's Max was always 999999, letting customers SELECT
                   past their group's limit and only get stopped by a backend
                   DomainException (surfaced as a generic error toast). The
                   UI now clamps to the limit like the Products grid does. *@
                <div class="purchase-row">
                    <RadzenNumeric @bind-Value="_quantity"
                                   Min="1"
                                   Max="@(_myPurchaseLimit ?? 999999)"
                                   Step="1"
                                   Style="width: 100px;"
                                   class="qty-input" />
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["AddToCart"]"
                                  Icon="add_shopping_cart"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                  Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                  class="add-to-cart-btn"
                                  Disabled="@(_isSubmitting)"
                                  Click="@HandleAddToCartAsync" />
                </div>

                @if (_myPurchaseLimit.HasValue)
                {
                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                        @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["MyPurchaseLimitHint"], _myPurchaseLimit.Value)
                    </RadzenText>
                }

                @* ── STAFF EDIT SECTION ──
                   Only shown to Admin / Manager / Employee. Contains:
                     1. Inline edit of Name + Description with Save button.
                     2. Per-group purchase limits editor.
                   The photo editor opens as a separate modal-like card above
                   (controlled by _isPhotoEditorOpen). All edits dispatch
                   Wolverine commands; the backend [RequireRoles] attribute
                   is the authoritative gate — the UI check just hides the
                   affordance for non-staff. *@
                @if (_canEdit)
                {
                    <div class="staff-section">
                        <div class="staff-section-title">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="edit" />
                            <span>@Loc["StaffEditTitle"]</span>
                        </div>

                        @* Inline edit: Name + Description + Save button.
                           Editable copies are held in _editName / _editDescription
                           so the user can type freely without committing on each
                           keystroke. Save dispatches UpdateProductDetailsCommand
                           with the new values + the EXISTING picture URL + price
                           (we don't touch those here). *@
                        <div class="edit-row">
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldName"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_editName"
                                               TValue="string"
                                               Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                        </div>
                        <div class="edit-row">
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldDescription"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenTextArea @bind-Value="_editDescription"
                                                TValue="string"
                                                Rows="3"
                                                Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                        </div>
                        <div class="edit-actions">
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SaveDetails"]"
                                          Icon="save"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Disabled="@(_isSavingDetails || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_editName))"
                                          Click="@HandleSaveDetailsAsync" />
                        </div>

                        @* ── Per-group purchase limits editor ──
                           Shows ALL existing group names with their current
                           limits (or an empty input if no limit is set).
                           Each row has:
                             - Group name (read-only)
                             - Limit input (RadzenNumeric, min=1, max=1_000_000)
                             - "Save" button → SetProductPurchaseLimitCommand
                             - "Remove" button (only when a limit exists) →
                               RemoveProductPurchaseLimitCommand
                           Plus an "Add custom group" button below for groups
                           that don't exist yet (forward-looking). *@
                        <div class="staff-section-title" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="rule" />
                            <span>@Loc["PurchaseLimitsTitle"]</span>
                        </div>
                        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                            @Loc["PurchaseLimitsHint"]
                        </RadzenText>

                        @if (_isLoadingGroups)
                        {
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                @Loc["LoadingGroups"]
                            </RadzenText>
                        }
                        else if (_limitRows.Count == 0)
                        {
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                @Loc["NoLimitRows"]
                            </RadzenText>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            @foreach (var row in _limitRows)
                            {
                                <div class="limit-row">
                                    <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldLimitGroup"]"
                                                     Style="flex: 1 1 200px; min-width: 160px;">
                                        @if (row.IsExistingGroup)
                                        {
                                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1"
                                                        Style="display: block; padding: 0.5rem 0; font-weight: 600;">
                                                @row.GroupName
                                            </RadzenText>
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="row.GroupName"
                                                           TValue="string"
                                                           Placeholder="@Loc["LimitGroupPlaceholder"]"
                                                           Style="width: 100%;" />
                                        }
                                    </RadzenFormField>
                                    <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldLimitValue"]"
                                                     Style="flex: 0 1 140px; min-width: 100px;">
                                        <RadzenNumeric @bind-Value="row.Limit"
                                                       TValue="int?"
                                                       Min="1"
                                                       Max="1000000"
                                                       Placeholder="@Loc["LimitValuePlaceholder"]"
                                                       Style="width: 100%;" />
                                    </RadzenFormField>
                                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SaveLimit"]"
                                                  Icon="save"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                  Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                                  Disabled="@(!row.Limit.HasValue || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(row.GroupName) || row.IsSaving)"
                                                  Click="@(() => HandleSaveLimitAsync(row))" />
                                    @if (!row.IsCustom)
                                    {
                                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RemoveLimit"]"
                                                      Icon="delete"
                                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                      Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                      Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                                      Disabled="@(!row.HasExistingLimit || row.IsSaving)"
                                                      Click="@(() => HandleRemoveLimitAsync(row))" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <RadzenButton Icon="delete"
                                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                      Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                      Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                                      Click="@(() => _limitRows.Remove(row))"
                                                      AriaLabel="@Loc["RemoveLimit"]" />
                                    }
                                </div>
                            }
                        }

                        <div style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["AddCustomGroupRow"]"
                                          Icon="group_add"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                          Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                          Disabled="@_isLoadingGroups"
                                          Click="@AddCustomLimitRow" />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    }

    @* ── Photo editor (modal-like card) ──
       Opens when staff clicks "Change Photo" on the picture. Mirrors the
       CreateProduct.razor picture dropzone + preview card UI. The user
       picks a file, sees a preview, then clicks "Save photo" to:
         1. Upload the new file via IFileStorage.SaveAsync.
         2. Hard-delete the OLD file via IFileStorage.DeleteAsync.
         3. Dispatch UpdateProductDetailsCommand with the new PictureUrl.
       Cancel closes the editor without saving. Same validation rules as
       CreateProduct: JPEG/PNG/WebP only, 5 MB max. *@
    @if (_isPhotoEditorOpen && _product is not null)
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--rz-primary);">
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="photo_camera" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["ChangePhotoTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
                <RadzenButton Icon="close"
                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                              Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                              Style="margin-inline-start: auto;"
                              Click="@(() => _isPhotoEditorOpen = false)"
                              AriaLabel="@Loc["ClosePhotoEditor"]" />
            </RadzenStack>

            <div class="upload-section">
                @if (_selectedFile is null)
                {
                    <label class="picture-dropzone">
                        <InputFile OnChange="@OnInputFileChange"
                                   accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp"
                                   class="picture-dropzone-input" />
                        <div class="picture-dropzone-body">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="cloud_upload"
                                        Style="font-size: 2.5rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                            <div class="picture-dropzone-text">
                                <span class="picture-dropzone-title">@Loc["UploadDropzoneTitle"]</span>
                                <span class="picture-dropzone-hint">@Loc["UploadDropzoneHint"]</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </label>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="upload-card">
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_previewDataUrl))
                        {
                            <img src="@_previewDataUrl" alt="preview" class="upload-preview" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <div class="upload-preview-placeholder">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="image" />
                            </div>
                        }
                        <div class="upload-info">
                            <div class="file-name">@_selectedFile.Name</div>
                            <div class="file-size">@FormatBytes(_selectedFile.Size)</div>
                        </div>
                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RemoveImage"]"
                                      Icon="delete"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                      Click="@RemoveSelectedImage" />
                    </div>
                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block;">
                        @Loc["PictureHint"]
                    </RadzenText>
                }

                @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_uploadError))
                {
                    <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["UploadErrorTitle"]"
                                 Text="@_uploadError"
                                 AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                 Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                 ShowIcon="true" />
                }

                <div class="edit-actions">
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CancelPhotoEditor"]"
                                  Icon="close"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                  Disabled="@(_isSavingPhoto)"
                                  Click="@(() => _isPhotoEditorOpen = false)" />
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SavePhoto"]"
                                  Icon="save"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                  Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                  Disabled="@(_selectedFile is null || _selectedFileBytes is null || _isSavingPhoto)"
                                  Click="@HandleSavePhotoAsync" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </RadzenCard>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── Route parameter ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    [Parameter]
    public Guid Id { get; set; }

    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private ProductDto? _product;
    private string? _categoryHierarchy;
    private string? _loadError;
    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private int _quantity = 1;
    private bool _isSubmitting;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user is in Admin/Manager/Employee role. Computed
    /// once in OnInitializedAsync via AuthenticationStateProvider (NOT
    /// ICurrentUserService.IsInRole — see the file header for why).
    /// Gates the entire staff-edit section + the Change Photo button.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canEdit;

    /// <summary>
    /// The current user's per-product purchase limit, if any. Null means
    /// no limit applies (staff user, or customer in a group with no limit
    /// set on this product). Used to clamp the quantity selector's Max.
    /// </summary>
    private int? _myPurchaseLimit;

    // ── Editable copies for the Name/Description inline editor ──

    private string _editName = string.Empty;
    private string _editDescription = string.Empty;
    private bool _isSavingDetails;

    // ── Photo editor state ──
    //
    // Mirrors CreateProduct.razor's pattern. The file is buffered in
    // memory immediately in OnInputFileChange (NOT at submit time) to
    // avoid the JSException that occurs when the JS-side _blazorFilesById
    // registry is cleared by Hot Reload / circuit reconnect / runtime
    // housekeeping.

    private bool _isPhotoEditorOpen;
    private IBrowserFile? _selectedFile;
    private byte[]? _selectedFileBytes;
    private string? _previewDataUrl;
    private string? _uploadError;
    private bool _isSavingPhoto;

    private const long MaxFileSize = 5 * 1024 * 1024; // 5 MB

    private static readonly HashSet<string> AllowedContentTypes = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
    {
        "image/jpeg", "image/png", "image/webp"
    };

    // ── Purchase-limit editor state ──

    /// <summary>
    /// One row per group, existing or custom. Loaded once on page init
    /// by combining GetAllGroupNamesQuery (every existing group) with
    /// the product's existing limits (so each row shows its current
    /// value, or an empty input if no limit is set yet).
    /// </summary>
    private List<LimitRow> _limitRows = new();
    private bool _isLoadingGroups = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// One row in the per-group purchase-limit editor. Each row maps to
    /// either a SetProductPurchaseLimitCommand (when "Save" is clicked
    /// with a non-empty limit) or a RemoveProductPurchaseLimitCommand
    /// (when "Remove" is clicked — only available for existing-group
    /// rows that currently have a limit).
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class LimitRow
    {
        public string GroupName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
        public int? Limit { get; set; }

        /// <summary>
        /// True for rows seeded from GetAllGroupNamesQuery (every existing
        /// group must always be shown — name is read-only, row can't be
        /// deleted, but the limit can be set/changed/removed).
        /// False for rows added via "Add custom group" (name is editable,
        /// row can be deleted via the trash icon).
        /// </summary>
        public bool IsExistingGroup { get; set; }

        /// <summary>
        /// True for custom (new) rows added via the "Add custom group"
        /// button. False for existing-group rows.
        /// </summary>
        public bool IsCustom => !IsExistingGroup;

        /// <summary>
        /// True if this group currently has a limit set on this product
        /// (loaded from _product.PurchaseLimits at init time). Drives the
        /// enabled state of the "Remove" button.
        /// </summary>
        public bool HasExistingLimit { get; set; }

        /// <summary>
        /// True while a Save or Remove command is in flight for this row.
        /// Disables both buttons to prevent double-clicks.
        /// </summary>
        public bool IsSaving { get; set; }
    }

    // ── Lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Resolve role + (if staff) limit-editor data alongside the product
        // load. All three are independent reads.
        try
        {
            await ResolveRoleAsync();
            await LoadProductAsync();

            // After product loads, fire the category lookup + (for staff)
            // the group-names lookup in parallel.
            if (_product is not null)
            {
                _editName = _product.Name;
                _editDescription = _product.Description;
                // _myPurchaseLimit is now populated from the DTO (set by
                // GetProductByIdQueryHandler). Before this fix, it was
                // hardcoded to null because ProductDto didn't expose the
                // field — see the purchase-row comment above for the full
                // rationale on why this matters.
                _myPurchaseLimit = _product.MyPurchaseLimit;

                var categoryTask = LoadCategoryHierarchyAsync();
                var groupsTask = _canEdit ? LoadGroupNamesAsync() : Task.CompletedTask;
                await Task.WhenAll(categoryTask, groupsTask);
            }
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    private async Task ResolveRoleAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
            var user = authState.User;
            _canEdit = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin)
                       || user.IsInRole(Roles.Manager)
                       || user.IsInRole(Roles.Employee);
        }
        catch
        {
            // Safe fallback — if role resolution fails, treat as non-staff.
            // The backend handlers ALSO enforce [RequireRoles] as
            // defense-in-depth, so even if a non-staff user could see the
            // buttons, the dispatch would be rejected.
            _canEdit = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadProductAsync()
    {
        var query = new GetProductByIdQuery { ProductId = Id };
        var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<ProductDto>>(query);

        if (result.IsSuccess)
        {
            _product = result.Value;
        }
        else
        {
            _loadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Loads the full category hierarchy (Category › SubCategory › SubSubCategory)
    /// for the product's CategoryId. Non-fatal — if the lookup fails, the
    /// breadcrumb just shows "Products / [Product]" without the category.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task LoadCategoryHierarchyAsync()
    {
        if (_product is null || _product.CategoryId == Guid.Empty)
        {
            return;
        }

        try
        {
            var query = new GetCategoryByIdWithHierarchyQuery { CategoryId = _product.CategoryId };
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<CategoryDto>>(query);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                var cat = result.Value;
                var parts = new List<string> { cat.Name };

                if (_product.SubCategoryId.HasValue)
                {
                    var sub = cat.SubCategories.FirstOrDefault(s => s.Id == _product.SubCategoryId.Value);
                    if (sub is not null)
                    {
                        parts.Add(sub.Name);

                        if (_product.SubSubCategoryId.HasValue)
                        {
                            var subsub = sub.SubSubCategories.FirstOrDefault(ss => ss.Id == _product.SubSubCategoryId.Value);
                            if (subsub is not null)
                            {
                                parts.Add(subsub.Name);
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                _categoryHierarchy = string.Join(" › ", parts);
            }
            // Non-fatal.
        }
        catch
        {
            // Swallow — breadcrumb is purely a UI nicety.
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Loads all existing customer group names + seeds one LimitRow per
    /// group (existing-group rows). For each row that matches an existing
    /// limit on this product, pre-populates the Limit + sets HasExistingLimit
    /// so the Remove button is enabled.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task LoadGroupNamesAsync()
    {
        _isLoadingGroups = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<List<string>>>(
                new GetAllGroupNamesQuery());

            var groupNames = (result.IsSuccess && result.Value is not null)
                ? result.Value
                : new List<string>();

            // Build a lookup of existing limits on this product for quick
            // matching by group name (case-sensitive, matching the domain).
            var existingLimits = _product?.PurchaseLimits ?? new List<ProductPurchaseLimitDto>();
            var existingByGroup = existingLimits.ToDictionary(l => l.GroupName, l => l.Limit, StringComparer.Ordinal);

            foreach (var name in groupNames)
            {
                var hasLimit = existingByGroup.TryGetValue(name, out var limit);
                _limitRows.Add(new LimitRow
                {
                    GroupName = name,
                    Limit = hasLimit ? limit : null,
                    IsExistingGroup = true,
                    HasExistingLimit = hasLimit
                });
            }

            // Also add custom rows for any product limit whose group name
            // doesn't exist in GetAllGroupNamesQuery's result (e.g. the
            // group was deleted but the limit remains, or the limit was
            // set for a forward-looking group name that has no users yet).
            foreach (var limit in existingLimits)
            {
                if (!groupNames.Contains(limit.GroupName, StringComparer.Ordinal))
                {
                    _limitRows.Add(new LimitRow
                    {
                        GroupName = limit.GroupName,
                        Limit = limit.Limit,
                        IsExistingGroup = true, // treat as existing — limit is set
                        HasExistingLimit = true
                    });
                }
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Silent failure — the limits editor just shows empty.
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoadingGroups = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Add-to-cart ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task HandleAddToCartAsync()
    {
        if (_product is null || _quantity < 1)
        {
            return;
        }

        _isSubmitting = true;
        try
        {
            var command = new CreateOrAppendSaleCommand(_product.Id, _quantity);
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<Guid>>(command);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["AddedToCart"], _quantity, _product.Name),
                    summary: Loc["AddedToCartTitle"]);
                _quantity = 1;
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(
                    result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericAdd"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["Error_GenericAdd"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSubmitting = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Save Name + Description ────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Saves the editable Name + Description fields. Dispatches
    /// UpdateProductDetailsCommand with the new values + the EXISTING
    /// PictureUrl + Price (this command is the only one that can change
    /// PictureUrl, but we don't touch it here — picture changes go through
    /// the dedicated photo editor).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleSaveDetailsAsync()
    {
        if (_product is null || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_editName))
        {
            return;
        }

        _isSavingDetails = true;
        try
        {
            var command = new UpdateProductDetailsCommand(
                ProductId: _product.Id,
                Name: _editName.Trim(),
                Description: _editDescription.Trim(),
                PictureUrl: _product.PictureUrl,
                Price: _product.Price);

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(command);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                // Reflect the change locally so the read-only display updates
                // without a full reload. ProductDto is a class (not a record),
                // so we can't use `with` — create a new instance copying the
                // fields, overwriting Name + Description with the new values.
                _product = new ProductDto
                {
                    Id = _product.Id,
                    Name = _editName.Trim(),
                    Description = _editDescription.Trim(),
                    PictureUrl = _product.PictureUrl,
                    Price = _product.Price,
                    StockQuantity = _product.StockQuantity,
                    CategoryId = _product.CategoryId,
                    SubCategoryId = _product.SubCategoryId,
                    SubSubCategoryId = _product.SubSubCategoryId,
                    PurchaseLimits = _product.PurchaseLimits
                };
                await Toast.Success(Loc["DetailsSaved"], summary: Loc["DetailsSavedTitle"]);
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericSave"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["Error_GenericSave"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSavingDetails = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Save Photo (upload new + delete old) ───────────────────────────

    private async Task OnInputFileChange(InputFileChangeEventArgs e)
    {
        _uploadError = null;

        if (e.FileCount == 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        var file = e.File;

        if (!AllowedContentTypes.Contains(file.ContentType))
        {
            _uploadError = Loc["UploadInvalidType"];
            ClearSelectedFile();
            return;
        }

        if (file.Size > MaxFileSize)
        {
            _uploadError = Loc["UploadInvalidSize"];
            ClearSelectedFile();
            return;
        }

        _selectedFile = file;

        try
        {
            await using var readStream = file.OpenReadStream(maxAllowedSize: MaxFileSize);
            using var ms = new MemoryStream();
            await readStream.CopyToAsync(ms);
            _selectedFileBytes = ms.ToArray();
        }
        catch
        {
            _uploadError = Loc["UploadErrorGeneric"];
            ClearSelectedFile();
            return;
        }

        _previewDataUrl = await GeneratePreviewDataUrlAsync(file);
    }

    private async Task<string?> GeneratePreviewDataUrlAsync(IBrowserFile file)
    {
        try
        {
            var resized = await file.RequestImageFileAsync(file.ContentType, 400, 400);
            await using var stream = resized.OpenReadStream(maxAllowedSize: 2 * 1024 * 1024);
            using var ms = new MemoryStream();
            await stream.CopyToAsync(ms);
            var base64 = Convert.ToBase64String(ms.ToArray());
            return $"data:{file.ContentType};base64,{base64}";
        }
        catch
        {
            return null;
        }
    }

    private void ClearSelectedFile()
    {
        _selectedFile = null;
        _selectedFileBytes = null;
        _previewDataUrl = null;
    }

    private void RemoveSelectedImage()
    {
        ClearSelectedFile();
        _uploadError = null;
    }

    private static string FormatBytes(long bytes)
    {
        string[] units = { "B", "KB", "MB", "GB" };
        double size = bytes;
        int unit = 0;
        while (size >= 1024 && unit < units.Length - 1)
        {
            size /= 1024;
            unit++;
        }
        return $"{size:0.#} {units[unit]}";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Saves the selected photo:
    ///   1. Upload the new file via IFileStorage.SaveAsync → get new URL.
    ///   2. Hard-delete the OLD file via IFileStorage.DeleteAsync (the
    ///      previous PictureUrl). This is the "delete old + replace new"
    ///      behavior the user requested. DeleteAsync is best-effort and
    ///      idempotent — if the old file is already gone or the URL is
    ///      external, it silently no-ops.
    ///   3. Dispatch UpdateProductDetailsCommand with the new PictureUrl +
    ///      the existing Name/Description/Price (we don't touch those here).
    ///   4. Reflect the new PictureUrl locally + close the photo editor.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleSavePhotoAsync()
    {
        if (_product is null || _selectedFile is null || _selectedFileBytes is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        _isSavingPhoto = true;
        try
        {
            // Phase 1: upload new file.
            string? newUrl;
            try
            {
                using var stream = new MemoryStream(_selectedFileBytes, writable: false);
                newUrl = await FileStorage.SaveAsync(
                    stream,
                    _selectedFile.Name,
                    _selectedFile.ContentType,
                    CancellationToken.None);
            }
            catch (System.IO.InvalidDataException ex)
            {
                _uploadError = ex.Message;
                return;
            }
            catch (Exception)
            {
                _uploadError = Loc["UploadErrorGeneric"];
                return;
            }

            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(newUrl))
            {
                _uploadError = Loc["UploadErrorResponseFormat"];
                return;
            }

            // Phase 2: hard-delete the OLD file (if any). Best-effort —
            // DeleteAsync logs but doesn't throw on failure. Done BEFORE
            // updating the DB so we don't end up with a stale DB pointer
            // to a file that's been deleted (if DeleteAsync failed we'd
            // still have the new URL, so the worst case is an orphaned
            // old file — which is what we're trying to avoid, but it's
            // a non-fatal orphan).
            var oldUrl = _product.PictureUrl;
            if (!string.Equals(oldUrl, newUrl, StringComparison.Ordinal))
            {
                try { await FileStorage.DeleteAsync(oldUrl, CancellationToken.None); }
                catch { /* best-effort — DeleteAsync already logs */ }
            }

            // Phase 3: dispatch UpdateProductDetailsCommand with the new URL.
            var command = new UpdateProductDetailsCommand(
                ProductId: _product.Id,
                Name: _product.Name,
                Description: _product.Description,
                PictureUrl: newUrl,
                Price: _product.Price);

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(command);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                // Reflect the new PictureUrl locally. ProductDto is a class,
                // so we create a new instance copying the existing fields and
                // overwriting PictureUrl with the new URL.
                _product = new ProductDto
                {
                    Id = _product.Id,
                    Name = _product.Name,
                    Description = _product.Description,
                    PictureUrl = newUrl,
                    Price = _product.Price,
                    StockQuantity = _product.StockQuantity,
                    CategoryId = _product.CategoryId,
                    SubCategoryId = _product.SubCategoryId,
                    SubSubCategoryId = _product.SubSubCategoryId,
                    PurchaseLimits = _product.PurchaseLimits
                };
                ClearSelectedFile();
                _isPhotoEditorOpen = false;
                await Toast.Success(Loc["PhotoSaved"], summary: Loc["PhotoSavedTitle"]);
            }
            else
            {
                // The DB update failed — the new file is already on disk.
                // Log a warning but don't auto-clean it up (it'll be an
                // orphan, but that's better than a race where we delete a
                // file that was somehow concurrently referenced).
                _uploadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericSave"];
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            _uploadError = Loc["Error_GenericSave"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSavingPhoto = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Purchase-limit editor handlers ─────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Adds a new custom (empty) row to the limits editor. The user types
    /// a group name that doesn't exist yet (forward-looking — a limit can
    /// be set for a group before any users are in it). Custom rows can be
    /// removed via the trash icon; existing-group rows cannot.
    /// </summary>
    private void AddCustomLimitRow()
    {
        _limitRows.Add(new LimitRow
        {
            GroupName = string.Empty,
            Limit = null,
            IsExistingGroup = false
        });
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Saves a single limit row. Dispatches SetProductPurchaseLimitCommand
    /// (which adds or replaces the limit for the given group). On success,
    /// marks the row as HasExistingLimit=true so the Remove button becomes
    /// available.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleSaveLimitAsync(LimitRow row)
    {
        if (_product is null || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(row.GroupName) || !row.Limit.HasValue)
        {
            return;
        }

        row.IsSaving = true;
        try
        {
            var command = new SetProductPurchaseLimitCommand(
                ProductId: _product.Id,
                GroupName: row.GroupName.Trim(),
                Limit: row.Limit.Value);

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(command);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                row.HasExistingLimit = true;
                row.IsExistingGroup = true; // once saved, treat as existing — name becomes read-only
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["LimitSaved"], row.GroupName, row.Limit.Value),
                    summary: Loc["LimitSavedTitle"]);
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericSave"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["Error_GenericSave"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            row.IsSaving = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Removes a single limit row. Dispatches RemoveProductPurchaseLimitCommand
    /// (which is idempotent — succeeds even if no limit exists for the group).
    /// On success, clears the limit value + sets HasExistingLimit=false so the
    /// Remove button greys out (but the row stays so the user can re-set the
    /// limit if they change their mind).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleRemoveLimitAsync(LimitRow row)
    {
        if (_product is null || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(row.GroupName))
        {
            return;
        }

        row.IsSaving = true;
        try
        {
            var command = new RemoveProductPurchaseLimitCommand(
                ProductId: _product.Id,
                GroupName: row.GroupName.Trim());

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(command);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                row.Limit = null;
                row.HasExistingLimit = false;
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["LimitRemoved"], row.GroupName),
                    summary: Loc["LimitRemovedTitle"]);
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericSave"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["Error_GenericSave"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            row.IsSaving = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Display helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a MoneyDto for display. IRR is converted to Toman (amount ÷ 10)
    /// and labelled "تومان" — matches the Products grid convention so a
    /// customer sees the same unit on the listing and the detail page.
    /// Other currencies pass through unchanged.
    /// </summary>
    private static string FormatPrice(MoneyDto price)
    {
        if (price is null) return "—";
        var isIrr = string.Equals(price.Currency, "IRR", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        var displayAmount = isIrr ? price.Amount / 10m : price.Amount;
        var amount = displayAmount.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture);
        var unit = isIrr ? "تومان" : price.Currency;
        return $"{amount} {unit}";
    }
}